    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d689">

                <pb facs="1362" n="1340" sameAs="frus:frus1946v01/pg1340"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">560.AL/7–2446: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Certain Diplomatic Officers
                    </hi><anchor n="80" xml:id="d689-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1946-07-24T08:00:00-04:00">July 24, 1946—8 a.
                            m</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>You wall shortly receive third person air mail instruction<anchor n="81"
                        xml:id="d689-f2"/> enclosing copies Draft Charter of International Trade
                    Organization and explanatory covering memo. After clearance from Dept, which you
                    will receive by telegraph, please hand copies Draft Charter to Fonoff together with statement along lines of
                    covering memo.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Byrnes</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d689-f1" n="80" type="source" xml:id="d689-f1-content">
                <p>Cabled to the other governments named in the February ECOSOC resolution as members of the Preparatory Committee for the
                    trade and employment conference.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d689-f2" n="81" xml:id="d689-f2-content">
                <p>Fourteen of the instructions were sent out under date of July 25 (560.AL/7–2546).
                    Four of the instructions, despatched to United States missions in the Western
                    Pacific and South African areas, were sent out under date of July 26
                    (560.AL/7–2646). These documents necessarily were received by the different
                    missions and so transmitted to the different governments at varying times. See
                    footnote 85, <ref target="#pg1342">p. 1342</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
